# miRNA Presentation Standards

## File Conventions

- Paste-ready content: `docs/presentation/slide-content.md`
- One `## Slide N: Title` heading per slide
- Bibliography: `docs/presentation/sources/bibliography.md`
- Assets: `docs/presentation/assets/`

## Content Limits

- Maximum **5 bullets** per slide
- Prefer diagrams over dense text on slides 12 and 13

## Required Distinctions

- Slides 3 and 11 must clearly separate prediction tools from validation databases
- Slide 10 must describe mirDIP as integrative, not a single algorithm

## Data-Driven Slides

- Slide 12: pull from `docs/research/score-comparison-matrix.md` — do not invent score ranges
- Slide 13: PTEN example — centerpiece explaining methodological disagreement
- Slide 15: why naive averaging fails; cite integration options from research

## Citations

- Every non-obvious claim needs a bibliography entry
- Include figure/diagram sources on References slide
